WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.530
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:00.800 --> 00:04.500
About two months into my third year of high school.

3
00:08.680 --> 00:09.680
[Watarai: Morning]

4
00:09.680 --> 00:11.980
[Can we walk home together today?]

5
00:15.010 --> 00:19.680
I've retired from the badminton team, and have more time to spend with Watarai.

6
00:21.780 --> 00:24.110
[By the way, can I set this selfie as my lock screen?]

7
00:32.240 --> 00:35.140
I feel like I'm on cloud nine.

8
00:35.140 --> 00:38.180
Hioki! Morning!

9
00:38.180 --> 00:39.300
Morning.

10
00:39.300 --> 00:41.490
Morning.

11
00:41.490 --> 00:43.590
Why do you look so giddy?

12
00:43.590 --> 00:45.570
No reason.

13
00:45.570 --> 00:47.500
Something's different about you today.

14
00:47.500 --> 00:49.080
Is it your hair?

15
00:49.080 --> 00:50.740
- It is! - Yeah, I set it.

16
00:50.740 --> 00:53.880
- Does it look weird? - No.

17
00:53.880 --> 00:54.980
I'm just surprised.

18
00:54.980 --> 00:56.960
- Same. - You're sparkling.

19
00:56.960 --> 00:58.610
- Exactly. - And your aura.

20
00:58.610 --> 01:00.780
It's all wham! Bam! Pow!

21
01:00.780 --> 01:02.650
But my personality hasn't changed, right?

22
01:02.650 --> 01:04.190
- Yeah. - I guess not.

23
01:04.190 --> 01:06.370
Actually, scratch that.

24
01:06.370 --> 01:07.930
You've become more selfish.

25
01:07.930 --> 01:09.070
True.

26
01:09.070 --> 01:11.290
- Selfish? - Yeah.

27
01:11.290 --> 01:16.090
It's nothing serious though. You just ask for more favors.

28
01:16.090 --> 01:18.010
For real?

29
01:18.880 --> 01:22.990
I guess Watarai is so selfless,

30
01:22.990 --> 01:25.920
that maybe it has affected my day-to-day actions?

31
01:28.490 --> 01:30.740
Sorry. Was I causing trouble?

32
01:30.740 --> 01:34.030
- No, no. - Not at all.

33
01:34.030 --> 01:36.420
Don't worry, your favors are nothing

34
01:36.420 --> 01:38.700
compared to Tsujitani's ridiculous ones.

35
01:38.700 --> 01:43.930
- Yeah. - Vroom, vroom, vroom!

36
01:43.930 --> 01:46.350
Speak of the devil.

37
01:47.010 --> 01:49.850
I forgot my necktie.

38
01:49.850 --> 01:52.390
- Someone lend me theirs! - See?

39
01:52.390 --> 01:55.300
We have no spares. Just accept your fate.

40
01:55.300 --> 01:58.090
Please, I'm begging you guys.

41
01:58.090 --> 01:59.960
Hioki.

42
01:59.960 --> 02:02.910
Please? I only need half.

43
02:02.910 --> 02:04.990
Split it in half with a scissors,

44
02:04.990 --> 02:07.230
like you would an eraser!

45
02:07.230 --> 02:09.090
This isn't like splitting an eraser.

46
02:09.090 --> 02:12.300
- Please? - Dude, cut it out!

47
02:12.300 --> 02:13.810
My necktie's gonna...

48
02:13.810 --> 02:16.070
Tsujitani.

49
02:17.410 --> 02:20.280
What are you doing to my Hioki?

50
02:20.280 --> 02:21.520
Come on.

51
02:21.520 --> 02:23.440
- Watarai's necktie... - No!

52
02:23.440 --> 02:26.280
A weakling like you stands no chance against him!

53
02:26.280 --> 02:27.500
Guys, no!

54
02:27.500 --> 02:29.170
Morning.

55
02:29.170 --> 02:30.950
Morning.

56
02:39.340 --> 02:41.650
There, all fixed.

57
02:41.650 --> 02:43.120
Thanks.

58
02:43.120 --> 02:45.200
You set your hair today?

59
02:45.200 --> 02:47.260
Yeah, with the oil you gave me.

60
02:47.260 --> 02:50.120
- Cute. - I'm wearing the belt, too. See?

61
02:50.120 --> 02:52.670
You are! I'm glad.

62
02:52.670 --> 02:54.450
It looks great.

63
02:55.790 --> 03:00.660
I was about to respond to your text. Yeah, we can walk home together.

64
03:00.660 --> 03:03.130
Okay. Then I'll come get you after class.

65
03:03.130 --> 03:04.600
Cool.

66
03:05.650 --> 03:08.230
See you later.

67
03:08.230 --> 03:09.920
Wait.

68
03:12.510 --> 03:14.290
Huh?

69
03:44.020 --> 03:45.760
See you later.

70
03:58.230 --> 04:02.070
I feel like I'm a bit too giddy.

71
04:06.890 --> 04:09.940
[Suzu Niiyama: Hey, Watarai!] [How are you doing?]

72
04:11.020 --> 04:12.860
Ah well.

73
04:14.300 --> 04:18.550
I can't help it if I'm happy.

74
05:22.720 --> 05:24.390
[After school]

75
05:24.390 --> 05:26.080
Hioki.

76
05:27.100 --> 05:28.120
Want to walk home together?

77
05:28.120 --> 05:31.700
Sorry, I have plans with Watarai today.

78
05:31.700 --> 05:32.820
Aw, too bad.

79
05:32.820 --> 05:34.100
Then we part ways here.

80
05:34.100 --> 05:36.300
- See you tomorrow. - See you.

81
05:36.300 --> 05:38.050
See you!

82
05:38.050 --> 05:39.250
Oh, hey!

83
05:39.250 --> 05:41.040
Looking good as ever.

84
05:41.040 --> 05:43.840
- You, too. - Hioki, are you free?

85
05:43.840 --> 05:45.100
Wanna grab a bite together?

86
05:45.100 --> 05:47.940
- Sorry, I have plans with Watarai. - Perfect!

87
05:47.940 --> 05:49.160
I'll call them over.

88
05:49.160 --> 05:51.770
Also, the impenetrable Sato is working today.

89
05:51.770 --> 05:53.900
- So, back me up, okay? - Sato?

90
05:53.900 --> 05:56.200
Haven't heard that name in a while.

91
05:59.350 --> 06:00.600
[Watarai: Sorry, I had plans come up] [I can't walk back with you today]

92
06:00.600 --> 06:03.050
[Watarai: I'm really sorry]

93
06:04.260 --> 06:06.470
Watarai says he can't join.

94
06:06.470 --> 06:08.830
Huh? Why?

95
06:08.830 --> 06:11.540
Hioki, apparently Watarai left already.

96
06:11.540 --> 06:14.300
Yeah, he just texted. Seems like something came up.

97
06:14.300 --> 06:15.860
He left in a hurry. What happened?

98
06:15.860 --> 06:18.400
I don't know. He didn't mention a reason.

99
06:18.400 --> 06:22.950
He prioritized something over you? That's unusual.

100
06:22.950 --> 06:25.820
- Seriously? Watarai? - What?

101
06:25.820 --> 06:30.370
My friend just saw Watarai walking home with a super cute girl!

102
06:30.370 --> 06:32.460
- What? - No way!

103
06:32.460 --> 06:34.280
Watarai had a girlfriend? [Respectful Watarai Fanclub]

104
06:34.280 --> 06:36.250
I had no idea! [Respectful Watarai Fanclub]

105
06:36.250 --> 06:38.060
I mean, I'm happy for him. [Respectful Watarai Fanclub]

106
06:38.060 --> 06:41.430
But what a shock!

107
06:42.600 --> 06:44.920
- Huh? - What's going on?

108
06:44.920 --> 06:48.420
Beats me. Must be a misunderstanding.

109
06:48.420 --> 06:50.240
I don't want to assume,

110
06:50.960 --> 06:52.960
but he better not be cheating on Hioki.

111
06:52.960 --> 06:55.380
You know he wouldn't.

112
06:55.380 --> 06:59.140
Yeah, but isn't it all too suspicious?

113
06:59.140 --> 07:02.480
Hioki, are you okay? Does it bother you?

114
07:02.480 --> 07:04.200
No, not at all.

115
07:04.200 --> 07:07.140
I'm sure this is just a misunderstanding.

116
07:07.140 --> 07:08.520
I'll ask them about it.

117
07:08.520 --> 07:10.560
No, you don't need to.

118
07:15.260 --> 07:18.030
According to that girl's testimony,

119
07:18.030 --> 07:20.410
they were seen around this area.

120
07:20.410 --> 07:23.080
Okay. Let's look for them.

121
07:23.080 --> 07:24.680
Hold on.

122
07:24.680 --> 07:26.350
We really don't need to be doing this.

123
07:26.350 --> 07:29.310
If you let this slide, it'll only bother you.

124
07:29.310 --> 07:30.870
You need to clear things up.

125
07:30.870 --> 07:32.820
But still...

126
07:34.530 --> 07:37.090
Let me make one thing clear.

127
07:37.090 --> 07:42.470
Friend or not, cheating is the one thing I'll never let slide.

128
07:42.470 --> 07:46.780
You don't have to join me, but I want to see the truth.

129
07:48.270 --> 07:50.270
Nakasato...

130
07:50.270 --> 07:53.270
He's totally traumatized by his ex-girlfriend.

131
07:53.270 --> 07:56.550
I'm sure those girls just saw the wrong guy.

132
07:56.550 --> 07:58.730
Yeah, I think so, too.

133
07:58.730 --> 08:01.280
Watarai would never...

134
08:01.280 --> 08:02.950
- Yeah. - He wouldn't.

135
08:02.950 --> 08:05.010
Found him!

136
08:05.010 --> 08:06.570
Come on, let's go.

137
08:11.040 --> 08:13.760
Quiet! Sneak over.

138
08:13.760 --> 08:16.480
Hurry, hurry!

139
08:17.410 --> 08:20.270
- What? - Where is he?

140
08:21.530 --> 08:24.590
There, right there.

141
08:24.590 --> 08:26.750
And look, in the back.

142
08:26.750 --> 08:28.840
- Watarai? - Shh!

143
08:31.960 --> 08:34.760
For real?

144
08:34.760 --> 08:38.060
What the... he can't be serious.

145
08:38.060 --> 08:41.170
I'll go pour water on his head.

146
08:41.170 --> 08:43.710
Calm down.

147
08:44.670 --> 08:48.300
Wait a sec, I've seen that girl before.

148
08:56.320 --> 08:57.870
Found her.

149
09:00.100 --> 09:02.760
Look. That's her.

150
09:02.760 --> 09:05.850
Right?

151
09:05.850 --> 09:07.780
I've seen that picture, too.

152
09:07.780 --> 09:10.270
I think she's...

153
09:10.270 --> 09:12.500
His ex-girlfriend.

154
09:23.850 --> 09:26.200
What now? Do we barge in to interrogate?

155
09:26.200 --> 09:28.100
No.

156
09:28.100 --> 09:31.520
They could just be friends.

157
09:31.520 --> 09:33.350
Maybe she needs his help.

158
09:33.350 --> 09:36.500
Yeah. I bet.

159
09:36.500 --> 09:41.780
Besides, Watarai would explain himself if you asked.

160
09:44.670 --> 09:46.400
Are you sure you're okay?

161
09:46.400 --> 09:47.980
Yeah.

162
09:47.980 --> 09:50.000
I'm fine.

163
09:53.180 --> 09:55.300
Or so I said, but...

164
09:55.300 --> 10:00.950
[Next morning]

165
10:01.850 --> 10:04.450
I might not be okay.

166
10:06.920 --> 10:09.870
What do you mean, "ex-girlfriend"?

167
10:09.870 --> 10:13.480
And why? I don't get it.

168
10:13.480 --> 10:15.770
Argh, I'm so curious...

169
10:15.770 --> 10:17.450
- Hioki! - Yes, sir?

170
10:17.450 --> 10:19.060
Why are you nuzzling the wall?

171
10:19.060 --> 10:20.820
Yeah, you okay?

172
10:20.820 --> 10:22.500
I'm totally fine.

173
10:22.500 --> 10:24.560
Really? I wonder.

174
10:24.560 --> 10:28.220
Hioki. Morning.

175
10:28.220 --> 10:29.850
Morning.

176
10:30.650 --> 10:33.370
Sorry about yesterday. Were you okay alone?

177
10:33.370 --> 10:36.320
Yeah. I hung out with the other guys.

178
10:36.320 --> 10:37.940
I see.

179
10:41.630 --> 10:45.520
Watarai, were you okay? I know something came up.

180
10:51.740 --> 10:53.490
Actually...

181
10:57.850 --> 11:00.800
Do you have time after school today?

182
11:04.390 --> 11:05.930
Yeah.

183
11:07.250 --> 11:09.730
Then can we walk home together?

184
11:10.440 --> 11:13.880
I need to tell you something.

185
11:25.200 --> 11:27.240
He's so picture perfect.

186
11:27.240 --> 11:29.400
I wish I could be that book.

187
11:29.400 --> 11:30.600
I want to be his headphones.

188
11:30.600 --> 11:33.490
It's definitely better to be the book!

189
11:35.290 --> 11:38.940
What does he need to tell me?

190
11:45.310 --> 11:46.860
Watarai.

191
11:46.860 --> 11:49.020
Could you help us with this problem?

192
11:49.020 --> 11:52.040
Sure. You use a new equation here...

193
11:52.040 --> 11:55.710
Now that I think about it...

194
11:59.070 --> 12:02.680
I never asked about his love life, did I?

195
12:02.680 --> 12:04.380
That was so easy to understand!

196
12:04.380 --> 12:06.370
- Thank you! - Thanks!

197
12:06.370 --> 12:09.260
- Good luck with the rest. - Thanks!

198
12:13.980 --> 12:15.150
Hioki.

199
12:15.150 --> 12:17.930
So, were you two able to talk?

200
12:17.930 --> 12:21.070
Not yet. We're gonna talk after school.

201
12:21.070 --> 12:22.780
I see.

202
12:22.780 --> 12:24.430
Actually, Hotta.

203
12:25.840 --> 12:27.770
Can I ask a question?

204
12:27.770 --> 12:29.290
Sure.

205
12:33.000 --> 12:35.530
So...

206
12:36.890 --> 12:41.160
Do you know why Watarai and his ex broke up?

207
12:41.160 --> 12:45.400
I don't know the exact details,

208
12:45.400 --> 12:47.790
but I did hear Watarai was the one who broke up with her.

209
12:47.790 --> 12:49.730
- I see. - Yeah.

210
12:49.730 --> 12:52.940
Apparently, his girlfriend's personality...

211
12:55.470 --> 12:58.510
It suddenly changed when they became high schoolers.

212
12:58.510 --> 13:00.680
- Her personality? - Yeah.

213
13:00.680 --> 13:04.580
That was apparently the last straw for him.

214
13:04.580 --> 13:07.070
At least, I think that was the reason.

215
13:08.340 --> 13:10.250
But my personality hasn't changed, right?

216
13:10.250 --> 13:11.790
- Yeah. - I guess not.

217
13:11.790 --> 13:13.950
Actually, scratch that.

218
13:13.950 --> 13:16.590
You've become more selfish.

219
13:17.870 --> 13:20.020
No way...

220
13:20.020 --> 13:22.420
- Something up? - No.

221
13:23.950 --> 13:28.520
Is Watarai over me because I became selfish?

222
13:34.190 --> 13:35.680
See you later.

223
13:54.930 --> 13:59.800
So, about what I wanted to tell you.

224
13:59.800 --> 14:01.300
Yeah.

225
14:03.490 --> 14:05.260
Hioki.

226
14:07.730 --> 14:10.890
I need to ask you for a favor.

227
14:14.990 --> 14:19.090
I really didn't want to ask you this, but...

228
14:20.830 --> 14:24.320
I knew it. This dour mood...

229
14:28.060 --> 14:30.080
I'm sorry.

230
14:31.710 --> 14:33.420
Would you...

231
14:36.810 --> 14:39.050
Is this really happening?

232
14:41.580 --> 14:43.350
Would you...

233
14:46.990 --> 14:49.300
Is he really going to break up with me?

234
14:53.690 --> 14:57.460
Would you come see my ex with me?

235
15:00.630 --> 15:02.190
Huh?

236
15:16.420 --> 15:18.850
I'm sorry if I surprised you with that.

237
15:20.460 --> 15:23.130
After our date the other day,

238
15:23.130 --> 15:27.010
I happened to bump into my ex-girlfriend.

239
15:27.750 --> 15:29.900
I knew it was you, Tsukasa!

240
15:29.900 --> 15:31.100
Are you alone?

241
15:31.100 --> 15:33.830
- If you're free... - Sorry.

242
15:33.830 --> 15:35.390
The bus is about to come.

243
15:35.390 --> 15:38.010
Oh, right.

244
15:39.230 --> 15:40.960
In that case...

245
15:41.670 --> 15:44.140
I'll text you so we can catch up.

246
15:44.140 --> 15:45.550
Huh?

247
15:48.730 --> 15:50.620
After that encounter,

248
15:50.620 --> 15:54.580
she texted me, saying she wanted to talk. [Suzu Niiyama: Hey, Watarai!]

249
15:54.580 --> 15:56.070
Of course, I turned her down,

250
15:56.070 --> 16:00.980
because I didn't want to worry you.

251
16:02.370 --> 16:04.230
But then,

252
16:04.230 --> 16:05.900
yesterday...

253
16:14.430 --> 16:17.190
[Sorry, I just really wanna talk.]

254
16:17.190 --> 16:19.330
[I only need five minutes. Is that okay?]

255
16:19.330 --> 16:21.410
[I'm actually in the area by your school...]

256
16:23.410 --> 16:26.640
I couldn't just ignore her, so...

257
16:30.160 --> 16:32.450
You like lattes, right?

258
16:32.450 --> 16:33.960
Yeah.

259
16:36.000 --> 16:37.740
Here.

260
16:37.740 --> 16:39.360
Thanks.

261
16:39.360 --> 16:41.580
You remembered.

262
16:43.100 --> 16:45.970
How's school been? Are you having fun?

263
16:45.970 --> 16:48.270
Yeah. I am.

264
16:48.270 --> 16:50.020
You attend a co-ed school, right?

265
16:50.020 --> 16:53.250
You must be crazy popular.

266
16:54.850 --> 16:56.520
- Suzu. - Yeah?

267
16:57.590 --> 16:59.970
What did you need to tell me?

268
16:59.970 --> 17:02.940
Right, sorry.

269
17:03.970 --> 17:07.420
Tsukasa, do you have a girlfriend right now?

270
17:09.950 --> 17:14.020
I am dating someone.

271
17:14.900 --> 17:17.130
Is she a schoolmate of yours?

272
17:17.130 --> 17:18.330
Yeah.

273
17:18.330 --> 17:21.130
What's she like? Do you have a picture of her?

274
17:29.510 --> 17:31.680
Why hide it?

275
17:31.680 --> 17:33.480
I'm not hiding it.

276
17:33.480 --> 17:35.530
Then show me.

277
17:35.530 --> 17:37.050
I can't.

278
17:37.050 --> 17:38.700
Why?

279
17:41.680 --> 17:43.760
I get it.

280
17:43.760 --> 17:45.860
You're actually single, aren't you?

281
17:45.860 --> 17:46.920
Huh?

282
17:46.920 --> 17:51.020
I mean, there are no pictures of any girls on your Insta either.

283
17:51.020 --> 17:53.390
I won't show you any pictures.

284
17:53.390 --> 17:57.400
If that's all, then I'm leaving.

285
18:01.580 --> 18:03.630
Bye.

286
18:03.630 --> 18:05.800
I want to give up on you.

287
18:08.280 --> 18:12.330
I still have feelings for you, Tsukasa.

288
18:13.870 --> 18:19.110
So, I want a reason to give up.

289
18:19.110 --> 18:23.040
If you can't show me a picture, can I meet her?

290
18:27.600 --> 18:29.630
Are you being serious?

291
18:30.420 --> 18:34.330
Please. I want to move on.

292
18:39.570 --> 18:41.190
Sorry.

293
18:41.190 --> 18:44.300
I should have told her "no" straight out.

294
18:44.990 --> 18:47.010
Don't apologize.

295
18:47.010 --> 18:49.440
It's not your fault.

296
18:51.140 --> 18:53.390
If anything,

297
18:53.390 --> 18:55.220
I'm also sorry.

298
18:55.840 --> 18:57.350
Huh?

299
19:00.300 --> 19:03.470
To tell you the truth,

300
19:03.470 --> 19:09.270
the other guys and I tailed you, and saw you with Suzu.

301
19:10.660 --> 19:12.740
You were watching us?

302
19:12.740 --> 19:14.540
Yeah. Sorry.

303
19:19.210 --> 19:20.880
Then...

304
19:22.550 --> 19:26.790
You must've been very anxious.

305
19:30.290 --> 19:32.580
A bit.

306
19:35.190 --> 19:37.200
I'm so sorry.

307
19:37.200 --> 19:39.150
It's all my fault.

308
19:41.150 --> 19:44.710
Don't blame yourself.

309
19:44.710 --> 19:47.510
I was overthinking things.

310
19:48.470 --> 19:52.480
Honestly, I thought I was getting dumped today.

311
19:55.850 --> 19:59.230
No. I'd never do that.

312
20:03.830 --> 20:06.980
I only care about you, Hioki.

313
20:07.950 --> 20:13.430
I don't plan on letting you go, ever.

314
20:22.040 --> 20:24.380
Phew...

315
20:26.800 --> 20:28.440
Are you relieved?

316
20:28.440 --> 20:30.010
Yeah.

317
20:32.940 --> 20:35.130
But will it really be okay?

318
20:35.800 --> 20:36.910
Huh?

319
20:36.910 --> 20:39.690
For me to meet your ex.

320
20:42.230 --> 20:43.880
Good point.

321
20:44.530 --> 20:47.840
I stubbornly made that choice in the moment,

322
20:47.840 --> 20:51.370
but we should carefully consider our next move.

323
20:52.450 --> 20:55.360
Yeah, let's think about it together.

324
20:55.360 --> 20:56.550
Thanks.

325
20:56.550 --> 20:58.000
Of course.

326
21:01.490 --> 21:03.440
Hey, I know.

327
21:03.440 --> 21:06.390
How about you come over, and we brainstorm a plan?

328
21:07.240 --> 21:09.150
Come over? To your place?

329
21:09.150 --> 21:10.660
Yeah.

330
21:10.660 --> 21:16.210
I think we could use the privacy.

331
21:16.210 --> 21:20.380
Will your folks be okay with me coming over uninvited?

332
21:20.380 --> 21:23.720
Don't worry about that. No one else is home today.

333
21:25.990 --> 21:27.770
No one?

334
21:27.770 --> 21:32.520
Yeah. So, if you're okay with it,

335
21:32.520 --> 21:34.370
do you want to come over?

336
21:42.690 --> 21:44.940
What a downpour!

337
21:46.990 --> 21:48.560
You okay?

338
21:52.410 --> 21:54.340
- Come on in. - Thanks.

339
21:54.340 --> 21:56.340
I'll go grab you a towel.

340
21:56.340 --> 21:57.860
Sure.

341
22:00.450 --> 22:03.100
I actually came over.

342
22:03.100 --> 22:05.440
We're only going to talk.

343
22:05.440 --> 22:08.960
No need to be nervous.

344
22:08.960 --> 22:11.050
But...

345
22:11.050 --> 22:12.530
Sorry I made you wait.

346
22:12.530 --> 22:14.230
It's fine.

347
22:15.610 --> 22:17.230
Thanks.

348
22:23.270 --> 22:24.860
Okay.

349
22:37.500 --> 22:40.120
What're you doing?

350
22:40.120 --> 22:41.680
Come on in.

351
22:42.500 --> 22:44.820
Thanks for having me.

352
22:46.380 --> 22:50.450
Alone, in Watarai's house.

353
22:50.450 --> 22:53.130
Will I really be okay?

354
22:56.100 --> 22:57.560
Yay! [First time at his boyfriend's house]

355
22:57.560 --> 22:58.820
No fair. [First time at his boyfriend's house]

356
22:58.820 --> 23:00.680
No! [First time at his boyfriend's house]

357
23:00.680 --> 23:02.770
Something I haven't told my parents...

358
23:02.770 --> 23:05.990
Have you ever thought about doing it with me?

359
23:05.990 --> 23:08.230
The thing about Watarai's ex...

360
23:08.230 --> 23:11.020
I want to stay by your side, Watarai.

361
23:11.020 --> 23:13.690
Please go out with me.

362
23:15.090 --> 23:17.000
I'll be okay.
